# Check every text file out with the same bytes on every platform.
#
# Two things in this repository depend on byte-for-byte identity across
# operating systems:
#
#   1. doctrine/manifest.md records a SHA-256 for each doctrine file, and the
#      roast lenses verify that digest before loading any guidance. Under a
#      CRLF checkout the bytes on disk differ from the bytes that were hashed,
#      every digest mismatches, and doctrine cannot load at all on Windows.
#
#   2. Tests that assert on file content match text that a CRLF checkout
#      rewrites, so assertions pass on Linux and macOS and fail on Windows for
#      a reason unrelated to what they are testing.
#
# Normalising to LF removes both problems at the source rather than teaching
# every reader and every assertion to tolerate two encodings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
